Description: Read template tags among attributes as attributes of their own
 Template characters never ended an attribute name, so in
 "<span {% if x %}class="a"{% endif %}>" the key was "{% if x %}class" and
 in "{{ a }}{% if b %} id="c"" the two templates merged into one key. Now a
 tag template is an attribute key of its own and ends any key it follows; a
 comment template between
 attributes is skipped like whitespace. A print still continues a key, as in
 "data-{{ name }}".
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/parse-for-eslint.test.ts ("Twig as part of the markup structure")
Last-Update: 2026-10-22
